NEW browser read access to one thread and a way to propose messages. Its tokens are HMACs of the thread and share id under a server key ([GuestShareService](../../apps/server/src/guest/GuestShareService.ts)), so nothing secret is stored. The share in the thread projection is the only state: replacing, closing, or archiving it revokes every token, and the orchestrator's serial commands make redeeming and sending happen once. Guest tokens never enter `SessionStore`, so no RPC, WebSocket, or MCP path can accept one. Guest routes also require T3 Connect to still serve the link's hostname; the request's Host header is not checked, because a LAN client can forge it. ### MCP clients are a separate audience Agents T3
